<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#frankokratia">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frankokratia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1204">1204</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Latinokratia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frankokratia ('rule of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a>') is the period of Western, chiefly French and Italian, rule in Greek lands after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a> of 1204. It covered the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a>, the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>, Venetian colonies and other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> states; most were lost to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> by the fifteenth century, though <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> held some islands much longer.</p></div>
